cite-title\">Phd.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">86d</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">οἱ \"τῶν ὁμοτίμων\" κ</span>. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Cyr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.1.9</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">κεκλημένος τινός</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">called from</b> or <b class=\"lex-tr\">after</b> him, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">P.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.67</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">καλεῖσθαι ἐπί τινι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">LXX</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ge.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">48.6</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">κέκληνται δέ σφιν ἕδραι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">O.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.76</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">2</span> <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Pass.</span> </span>, <b class=\"lex-tr\">to be called</b>, almost = εἰμί, esp. with words expressing kinship or status, <span class=\"gk\">ἐμὸς γαμβρὸς καλέεσθαι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.313</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">A.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pers.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2</span> </span> (anap.); <span class=\"gk\">ἀφνειοὶ καλέονται</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">15.433</span> </span>; esp. in <span class=\"lex-gram\">pf.</span> <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Pass.</span> </span> <span class=\"gk\">κέκλημαι, οὕνεκα σὴ παράκοιτις κέκλημαι</span> because I <b class=\"lex-tr\">am</b> thy wife, <span class=\"lex-ci